  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Folder Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the suggested folder structure, and I\'m finding it quite reasonable for a Vite-based single-page application. I am thinking of how this structure fits with a project that does not utilize Next.js 15, and is instead built around the former.\n\n\n**Defining Fonts and Design**\n\nI\'ve decided on Inter as the primary font and JetBrains Mono for a technical accent to achieve a premium, modern feel, appropriate for a dark-mode portfolio inspired by OpenAI, Anthropic, Vercel, Linear, and Stripe. I\'m focusing on incorporating these Google Fonts, and I\'m checking how to do this within the existing Tailwind v4 setup found in `src/index.css`. I\'m going to look next into adding custom Google fonts.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Variables**\n\nI\'m now ready to configure custom theme variables! I have decided to use the `@theme { ... }` syntax. I reviewed the existing `src/index.css` file and it only contains the `@import \"tailwindcss\";` line, so I\'ll add the theme configuration there. Next, I plan to create the `portfolioData.ts` file to store portfolio information. I also listed the sections I am going to need, starting with a sticky navbar and hero section. I will be sure to get the hero data completed, so I can set up my placeholders.\n\n\n**Generating Workspace Image**\n\nOkay, I\'m now setting up the image generation. I\'m focusing on creating an impactful placeholder image. The plan is to use our image generation tool with a detailed prompt for a minimalist, ultra-modern workspace to suit the dark theme. I\'ve considered parameters like aspect ratio and the desired file name, and am ready to design the code files. I\'m going to start by writing `src/data/portfolioData.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Portfolio Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the portfolio data structure. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of personal information, professional experience, and projects. Specifically, I\'m working to include details about Nivash\'s time at AstroVed Pvt. Ltd., to showcase his professional skills. The bullet points will highlight achievements like building LLM chains and agentic workflows. For the projects, I will detail his experience with an AI-Powered Numerology Prediction Platform, including problem, solution, and tech stack details.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Contributions**\n\nI\'m now detailing contributions to the AI-Powered Numerology Prediction Platform and the AI-Powered Astrology Services. For the numerology platform, I am highlighting my work on the calculation engine, LLM integration, and database optimization. For the astrology services, I\'m focusing on my role in the parsing pipeline, vector database queries, and the responsive UI, including the tech stacks I utilized.\n\n\n**Describing Agentic Workflow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the AI-Powered SEO Content Generation project. I focused on describing the problem it solves, which is helping marketing teams scale SEO content generation while maintaining quality and accuracy. I built an autonomous content generation workflow with AI Agents and Model Context Protocol (MCP) for research, content writing, and SEO scoring. My contribution was architecting the LangGraph workflow with dedicated research, writing, and auditing agents, along with the MCP servers to get live search trends, achieving a 40% speed boost. I utilized Python, LangGraph, Gemini API, and other relevant technologies.\n\n\n**Listing Tech Stack**\n\nI\'m now detailing the SDKs, covering backend with Node.js, Express, Python, FastAPI, and gRPC. I\'m also including databases like PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, MongoDB, and Firestore. For the frontend, I\'ll list React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion, along with HTML5/CSS3. Finally, I\'m noting the developer tools: Git, GitHub Actions, Docker, Vercel, AWS, and Postman. I am also planning how to integrate my career narrative, starting with my experience as an Associate AI Engineer.\n\n```\n**Analyzing Folder Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the suggested folder structure, and I\'m finding it quite reasonable for a Vite-based single-page application. I am thinking of how this structure fits with a project that does not utilize Next.js 15, and is instead built around the former.\n\n\n**Defining Fonts and Design**\n\nI\'ve decided on Inter as the primary font and JetBrains Mono for a technical accent to achieve a premium, modern feel, appropriate for a dark-mode portfolio inspired by OpenAI, Anthropic, Vercel, Linear, and Stripe. I\'m focusing on incorporating these Google Fonts, and I\'m checking how to do this within the existing Tailwind v4 setup found in `src/index.css`. I\'m going to look next into adding custom Google fonts.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Variables**\n\nI\'m now ready to configure custom theme variables! I have decided to use the `@theme { ... }` syntax. I reviewed the existing `src/index.css` file and it only contains the `@import \"tailwindcss\";` line, so I\'ll add the theme configuration there. Next, I plan to create the `portfolioData.ts` file to store portfolio information. I also listed the sections I am going to need, starting with a sticky navbar and hero section. I will be sure to get the hero data completed, so I can set up my placeholders.\n\n\n**Generating Workspace Image**\n\nOkay, I\'m now setting up the image generation. I\'m focusing on creating an impactful placeholder image. The plan is to use our image generation tool with a detailed prompt for a minimalist, ultra-modern workspace to suit the dark theme. I\'ve considered parameters like aspect ratio and the desired file name, and am ready to design the code files. I\'m going to start by writing `src/data/portfolioData.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Portfolio Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the portfolio data structure. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of personal information, professional experience, and projects. Specifically, I\'m working to include details about Nivash\'s time at AstroVed Pvt. Ltd., to showcase his professional skills. The bullet points will highlight achievements like building LLM chains and agentic workflows. For the projects, I will detail his experience with an AI-Powered Numerology Prediction Platform, including problem, solution, and tech stack details.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Contributions**\n\nI\'m now detailing contributions to the AI-Powered Numerology Prediction Platform and the AI-Powered Astrology Services. For the numerology platform, I am highlighting my work on the calculation engine, LLM integration, and database optimization. For the astrology services, I\'m focusing on my role in the parsing pipeline, vector database queries, and the responsive UI, including the tech stacks I utilized.\n\n\n**Describing Agentic Workflow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the AI-Powered SEO Content Generation project. I focused on describing the problem it solves, which is helping marketing teams scale SEO content generation while maintaining quality and accuracy. I built an autonomous content generation workflow with AI Agents and Model Context Protocol (MCP) for research, content writing, and SEO scoring. My contribution was architecting the LangGraph workflow with dedicated research, writing, and auditing agents, along with the MCP servers to get live search trends, achieving a 40% speed boost. I utilized Python, LangGraph, Gemini API, and other relevant technologies.\n\n**Listing Tech Stack**\n\nI\'m now detailing the SDKs, covering backend with Node.js, Express, Python, FastAPI, and gRPC. I\'m also including databases like PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, MongoDB, and Firestore. For the frontend, I\'ll list React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion, along with HTML5/CSS3. Finally, I\'m noting the developer tools: Git, GitHub Actions, Docker, Vercel, AWS, and Postman. I am also planning how to integrate my career narrative, starting with my experience as an Associate AI Engineer.\n```\n\n\n**Verifying